WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.279 --> 00:00:09.289
So I’ve been studying some Japanese Death
poems as I finish up my short film, Dreadful

00:00:09.289 --> 00:00:10.289
Misfortune.

00:00:10.289 --> 00:00:13.160
I’ll talk more about that in the coming
months.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.800
But with National Poetry Day coming up, I’m
doing this collab with Don’t Turn Around,

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.230
where we’ll be reading you some horror poetry.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:25.340
I thought it would be fun to practice writing
some Japanese Death Poems and put a CZsWorld

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.900
twist on it, so I’m gonna base each of these
poems on some of my favorite horror anime,

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.860
and whoever can guess what they’re from
will win some kind of shoutout or something.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.690
And stick around to the end where I’ll narrate
the Japanese Death Poem from my upcoming film,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:43.850
Dreadful Misfortune.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:49.050
Ichi
I opposed the move.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.920
Gazing on empty caskets.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.600
He inquired aloud.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.640
Aren’t you afraid of dying?

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.839
I’ve been dead for some time now.

00:01:01.839 --> 00:01:04.800
Ni

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.070
Monsters roam this world.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.540
But justice will come swiftly,
as with all monsters.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:24.350
I know this monster because,
in truth, I am that monster.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.960
San

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.590
The ninth grade, class three.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.149
Would be the last grade, for me.

00:01:32.149 --> 00:01:34.469
As with those before.

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:36.691
A curse to grea t to ignore.

00:01:36.691 --> 00:01:45.600
Ignore her, to live one more.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.470
Shi

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:52.689
Twelve contestants play.

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:56.140
A twisted and fatal game.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.920
When even peers lock.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.950
Even friendship goes to shame.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:07.460
She only has her, to blame.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.680
Go

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.510
The coffee’s a bit strong.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.340
And this date’s gone on too long.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.050
City lights so dim.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:22.360
Walk me home, they look so grim.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:26.930
Leaving half of me with him.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.510
Bonasu

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:37.640
The ink of this scribe,
is only seen in the eyes,

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:42.819
of shinigami,
who possess glowing white eyes.

00:02:42.819 --> 00:02:50.680
Dreadful misfortune, runs dry.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:54.530
The voice you heard in this video was Don’t
Turn Around.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:58.480
Click the link right here to listen to the
epic horror poem that I helped narrate on

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.480
their channel.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:04.730
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:08.150
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:10.479
Assuming, we both survive.

